her groups stay plain action items"},"683":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-24","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Optional leading `icon` per item; links (`href`) and disabled items"},"684":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-25","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Submenus via `SubmenuTrigger`"},"685":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-26","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Two sizes (`sm`, `md`); set `size` explicitly on each submenu `Menu`"},"686":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-27","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Usable anchored to a trigger or standalone (e.g. inside a bottom-sheet `Drawer`)"},"687":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-28","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#default","content":"A trigger with plain action items."},"688":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-29","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#controlled","content":"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."},"689":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-30","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#bottom-sheet","content":"On small screens a menu often reads better as a bottom sheet than an anchored\npopover. Since `Menu` works standalone, drop it into a bottom `Drawer`."},"690":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-31","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#groups","content":"Labeled groups separated by dividers, a multi-select checkbox group mixed with\nplain action groups, leading icons, a disabled item, and a link."},"691":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-32","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#multiple-selection","content":"A `MenuGroup` with `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` renders its items as checkboxes.\nDrive the checked items with `selectedKeys` + `onSelectionChange` or\nseed them uncontrolled with `defaultSelectedKeys`. Keys correspond to each\n`MenuItem`'s `id`."},"692":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-33","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#rich-content-from-an-item","content":"A `Menu` is a collection, so it only renders `MenuItem`, `MenuGroup`,\n`MenuSeparator`, and `SubmenuTrigger` children. Rich content inside a `Menu`\nor submenu is not supported. To show a `Calendar`, let the item close the\nmenu from `onAction` and open a separate `Popover` anchored to the trigger\nwith `triggerRef`."},"693":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-34","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#single-selection","content":"A `MenuGroup` with `selectionMode=\"single\"` lets one item be selected at a time.\nDrive it with `selectedKeys` + `onSelectionChange` or seed it uncontrolled with\n`defaultSelectedKeys`. Keys correspond to each `MenuItem`'s `id`."},"694":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-35","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#sizes","content":"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."},"695":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-36","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#submenu","content":"Nested menus via `SubmenuTrigger`."},"696":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-37","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"**Space/Enter**: activate an item; **Escape**: close"},"697":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-38","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"**Arrow Up/Down**: move between items; **Home/End**: first/last"},"698":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-39","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"**Arrow Right/Left**: open/close a submenu"},"699":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-40","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"**Type to select**: jump to a matching item (string labels are used as `textValue`)"},"700":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-41","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"Multi-select items use RAC's `menuitemcheckbox` role; the checkbox indicator is\ndecorative (`aria-hidden`) and the item owns interaction"},"701":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-42","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#best-practices","content":"Give each selectable `MenuItem` a stable `id`, and provide the `Menu` an\n`aria-label` when there is no visible label."},"702":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-43","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#best-practices","content":"Use a leading `icon` for recognition, not as the only label - keep a text label."},"703":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-44","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#best-practices","content":"Reserve checkbox groups for multi-select; use plain groups for one-shot actions."},"704":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-45","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#best-practices","content":"A `Menu` is a collection: it only renders `MenuItem`, `MenuGroup`,\n`MenuSeparator`, and `SubmenuTrigger`. For rich content (a `Calendar`, a form),\nclose the menu from `onAction` and open a separate `Popover` anchored with\n`triggerRef` instead of putting it in a submenu."},"705":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"page","content":"MetricsLockup","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup"},"706":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-0","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","content":"The MetricsLockup component displays a single metric with an optional title, info tooltip, trend indicator, and description."},"707":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-1","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#installation","content":"Installation"},"708":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-2","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#examples","content":"Examples"},"709":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-3","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#default","content":"Default"},"710":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-4","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#with-trend","content":"With Trend"},"711":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-5","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#compact","content":"Compact"},"712":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-6","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"713":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-7","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"714":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-8","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#aria","content":"ARIA"},"715":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-9","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"716":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-10","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#props","content":"Props"},"717":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-11","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","content":"MetricsLockup displays a metric value prominently, with an optional title and tooltip for context, an optional trend icon to show direction of change, and a description label below the value."},"718":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-12","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#default","content":"A metric with a title, info tooltip, value, and description."},"719":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-13","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#with-trend","content":"Use the `trend` prop to show a directional icon next to the description. Accepts `'positive'`, `'negative'`, or `'neutral'`."},"720":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-14","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#compact","content":"Use the `compact` prop to render the metric value and description inline rather than stacked."},"721":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-15","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Key"},"722":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-16","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Description"},"723":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-17","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Tab"},"724":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-18","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Moves focus to the info trigger button and shows the tooltip"},"725":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-19","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Escape"},"726":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-20","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Closes the tooltip"},"727":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-21","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#aria","content":"The info trigger button uses `aria-label=\"More information\"` to describe its purpose."},"728":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-22","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#aria","content":"The tooltip uses `role=\"tooltip\"` and is associated with the info trigger via `aria-describedby`."},"729":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-23","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#aria","content":"The info trigger has a minimum touch target of 44×44px, achieved via a CSS pseudo-element, to meet WCAG 2.5.5."},"730":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-24","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"Keep tooltip content concise and informative."},"731":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-25","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"The `data` prop accepts strings or numbers — format currency and percentages before passing them in."},"732":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-26","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"`titleInfo` requires `title` to be set — the info icon is contextually tied to the title label. If `title` is absent, `titleInfo` has no effect."},"733":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-27","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"`trend` is intended to accompany `description` to provide temporal context (e.g. \"↑ +3% vs. last month\"). A trend icon alone, with no description, leaves the direction unanchored (\"up since *when*?\"). If `description` is not provided, `trend` has no effect."},"734":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"page","content":"NumberField","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field"},"735":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-0","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field","content":"NumberField is a numeric input with optional label, description, error message, min/max/step, and increment/decrement stepper buttons. Use it in forms for quantities, amounts, or percentages."},"736":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-1","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#features","content":"Features"},"737":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-2","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#installation","content":"Installation"},"738":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-3","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#examples","content":"Examples"},"739":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-4","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#default","content":"Default"},"740":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-5","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#number-field-controlled","content":"Number Field Controlled"},"741":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-6","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#number-field-invalid","content":"Number Field Invalid"},"742":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-7","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#number-field-disabled","content":"Number Field Disabled"},"743":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-8","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#number-field-hide-stepper","content":"Number Field Hide Stepper"},"744":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-9","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#number-field-value-scale","content":"Number Field Value Scale"},"745":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-10","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#format-options-numbering-system","content":"Format options (numbering system)"},"746":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-11","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#number-field-sizes","content":"Number Field Sizes"},"747":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-12","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#text-steppers","content":"Text Steppers"},"748":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-13","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"749":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-14","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"750":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-15","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#aria-and-labeling","content":"ARIA and labeling"},"751":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-16","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#best-practices","content":"Best practices"},"752":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-17","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#props","content":"Props"},"753":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-18","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#features","content":"**Label, description, error**: Optional label, helper text, and error message"},"754":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-19","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#features","content":"**Steppers**: Increment and decrement buttons, or `hideStepper` for a plain numeric input"},"755":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-20","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#features","content":"**Composition**: To customize the interior (for example text steppers instead of `-` and `+` icons), pass `children` and compose `Label`, `Group`, `Input`, and `Button`"},"756":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-21","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#default","content":"Minimal usage with label, placeholder, and min/max."},"757":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-22","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#number-field-controlled","content":"Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state."},"758":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-23","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#number-field-invalid","content":"Use `isInvalid` with `errorMessage` for validation feedback."},"759":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-24","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#number-field-disabled","content":"Use `isDisabled` to prevent input."},"760":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-25","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#number-field-hide-stepper","content":"Use `hideStepper` to show only the input without +/- buttons."},"761":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-26","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#number-field-value-scale","content":"Use `minValue`, `maxValue`, and `step` to set the allowed values. Steps are calculated from the minimum value."},"762":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-27","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#format-options-numbering-system","content":"By default, NumberField displays the value using the numbering system for the user's locale. Use the `formatOptions` prop to override the numbering system by setting the Unicode numbering system locale extension."},"763":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-28","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#number-field-sizes","content":"Compare the supported `md` and `sm` visual sizes."},"764":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-29","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#text-steppers","content":"Compose with `children` to replace the stepper icons with your own content, such as text."},"765":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-30","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#keyboard","content":"When focus is in the input (and the field is not read-only), keyboard behavior follows common spinbutton-style conventions:"},"766":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-31","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#keyboard","content":"**Arrow Up** / **Arrow Down** (or **Up** / **Down**): increase or decrease by `step`"},"767":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-32","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#keyboard","content":"**Page Up** / **Page Down**: larger increase or decrease when supported"},"768":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-33","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#keyboard","content":"**Home** / **End**: jump to `minValue` or `maxValue` when those props are set"},"769":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-34","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#keyboard","content":"Stepper buttons are real buttons and follow standard button keyboard activation. Use &#x2A;*`incrementAriaLabel`*&#x2A; and &#x2A;*`decrementAriaLabel`** when the default labels are not enough in your locale or UI."},"770":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-35","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#aria-and-labeling","content":"The input is associated with the visible label and optional description and error content for assistive technologies."},"771":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-36","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#aria-and-labeling","content":"Invalid and required states are exposed to assistive technologies when you use `isInvalid`, `errorMessage`, and `isRequired`."},"772":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-37","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#aria-and-labeling","content":"Set &#x2A;*`isWheelDisabled`** if the value should not change when the user scrolls with a pointer wheel while the field is focused."},"773":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-38","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#best-practices","content":"Pair &#x2A;*`isInvalid`*&#x2A; with &#x2A;*`errorMessage`** so users get both visual and programmatic feedback."},"774":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-39","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#best-practices","content":"Remember valid steps start from &#x2A;*`minValue`**."},"775":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-40","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#best-practices","content":"Use &#x2A;*`isDisabled`*&#x2A; when the value cannot be changed; use &#x2A;*`isReadOnly`** when the value should be visible but not editable. Do not use them interchangeably."},"776":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-41","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#best-practices","content":"For currency or units, ensure &#x2A;*`formatOptions`** (and locale) match what users are allowed to type."},"777":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-42","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#props","content":"When `children` is passed, `NumberField` is composed. Use `variant=\"control\"` with `slot=\"decrement\"` and `slot=\"increment\"` on Button so the steppers still change the value. A composed `Group` inherits `size` and `isDisabled` from the field, so set them on `NumberField` and leave the interior to the markup."},"778":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-43","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#props","content":"The `NumberField` component accepts the following props:"},"779":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"page","content":"Pagination","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination"},"780":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-0","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination","content":"A pagination component with prev/next buttons and dot indicators, configurable page limits, and optional visibility of controls and dots"},"781":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-1","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#installation","content":"Installation"},"782":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-2","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#examples","content":"Examples"},"783":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-3","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#default","content":"Default"},"784":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-4","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"785":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-5","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#default-active","content":"Default Active"},"786":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-6","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#with-limit","content":"With Limit"},"787":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-7","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#onchange-event","content":"onChange Event"},"788":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-8","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pagination#props","content":"Props"},"789":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-9","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#default","content":"The default pagination is uncontrolled. It renders prev/next buttons and one dot per page. The `total` prop sets the number of items."},"790":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-10","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#controlled","content":"Pass `activeIndex` and `onChange` to control the active page externally."},"791":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-11","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#default-active","content":"Use `defaultActiveIndex` to set the starting page in uncontrolled mode."},"792":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-12","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#with-limit","content":"Limit the number of items shown per page. When `limit` is greater than 1, the number of pages (dots) is derived from `Math.ceil(total / limit)`. For example, 10 items with a limit of 3 produces 4 pages (dots)."},"793":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-13","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#onchange-event","content":"The `onChange` callback fires with the new page index whenever the user navigates."},"794":{"id":"/docs/components/popover","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"page","content":"Popover","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover"},"795":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-0","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover","content":"The Popover component is an overlay element positioned relative to a trigger element."},"796":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-1","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#installation","content":"Installation"},"797":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-2","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#examples","content":"Examples"},"798":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-3","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#default","content":"Default"},"799":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-4","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#custom-anchor","content":"Custom Anchor"},"800":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-5","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#title-and-close-button","content":"Title and Close Button"},"801":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-6","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"802":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-7","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"803":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-8","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#aria","content":"ARIA"},"804":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-9","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"805":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-10","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/popover#props","content":"Props"},"806":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-11","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover","content":"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."},"807":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-12","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#default","content":"Use it with `<PopoverTrigger>`, which wraps both the popover content and an interactive trigger element (for example, a `Button`)."},"808":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-13","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#custom-anchor","content":"To position a popover relative to a different element than its trigger, use the `triggerRef` and `isOpen` props instead of `<PopoverTrigger>`. `onOpenChange` is called when the user opens or closes the popover."},"809":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-14","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#title-and-close-button","content":"Add a `Heading slot=\"title\"` and a `CloseButton` for a titled, dismissible popover. The heading\nalso gives the dialog its accessible name."},"810":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-15","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Key"},"811":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-16","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Action"},"812":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-17","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"`Enter/Space`"},"813":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-18","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Opens the popover from its trigger"},"814":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-19","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"`Escape`"},"815":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-20","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Closes the popover"},"816":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-21","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#aria","content":"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"},"817":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-22","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#aria","content":"A `Heading slot=\"title\"` labels the dialog via `aria-labelledby`. Without one, a popover inside\na `PopoverTrigger` falls back to being labelled by its trigger; standing alone with\n`triggerRef` it needs an explicit `aria-label`"},"818":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-23","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#best-practices","content":"Pass an `aria-label` when anchoring with `triggerRef` instead of wrapping a `PopoverTrigger`,\nsince there is no trigger to borrow the name from."},"819":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-24","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#best-practices","content":"Popover width is determined by its content, and it's recommended to keep it under 400px."},"820":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-25","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#props","content":"The `Popover` component accepts the following props:"},"821":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-26","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#props","content":"The `PopoverTrigger` component accepts the following props:"},"822":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"page","content":"Pressable","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable"},"823":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-0","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable","content":"A wrapperless interaction primitive that adds accessible press behavior to a single child element."},"824":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-1","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Features"},"825":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-2","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#installation","content":"Installation"},"826":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-3","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#examples","content":"Examples"},"827":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-4","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#default","content":"Default"},"828":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-5","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#customization","content":"Customization"},"829":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-6","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"830":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-7","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"831":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-8","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"832":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-9","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#props","content":"Props"},"833":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-10","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Adds accessible press behavior to an existing visual component."},"834":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-11","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Applies interaction states directly to the child without adding a wrapper element."},"835":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-12","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Supports pointer, touch, and keyboard interactions through React Aria."},"836":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-13","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Preserves the child's layout, shape, and base visual styling while adding state feedback."},"837":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-14","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#default","content":"Add accessible press behavior to an existing visual component without adding a wrapper element.\nThe surface supports pointer, touch, and keyboard activation."},"838":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-15","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#customization","content":"Use `Pressable` when an existing visual component or layout surface needs press behavior while keeping its own DOM element, layout, and styles. The child must be a single element that forwards its ref and accepts the DOM, ARIA, and event props supplied by React Aria."},"839":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-16","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#customization","content":"Use `Button` when you need a standard button control with button-specific sizing, layout, and visual variants."},"840":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-17","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#customization","content":"Pass `onPress` for the action instead of wiring separate pointer and keyboard handlers:"},"841":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-18","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#accessibility","content":"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."},"842":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-19","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#accessibility","content":"Use a semantic interactive element when possible. For a non-semantic child such as `Avatar` or `Box`, provide an appropriate interactive role and an accessible name. Pressable makes the child focusable when the required props are forwarded."},"843":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-20","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#accessibility","content":"Do not add `role=\"button\"` to a native `<button>` or `<a>` unless you intentionally need to change its semantics. Use a dedicated semantic component such as `Button`, `LinkButton`, `Menu`, or `ToggleButton` when that control's meaning is known."},"844":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-21","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#best-practices","content":"Prefer a native interactive element or a semantic Antares component when the interaction meaning is known."},"845":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-22","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#best-practices","content":"Avoid nesting interactive elements inside the child passed to `Pressable`."},"846":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-23","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#best-practices","content":"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."},"847":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-24","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#troubleshooting","content":"If React Aria warns that the child must be focusable, ensure it is a single element that forwards its ref, `tabIndex`, DOM props, and ARIA attributes."},"848":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-25","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#troubleshooting","content":"If `onPress` does not fire, confirm that the child forwards event handlers and is not disabled by another component."},"849":{"id":"/docs/components/modal","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"page","content":"Modal","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal"},"850":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-0","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal","content":"The Modal component presents a dialog window over the page that focuses the user's attention on a single task or piece of information."},"851":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-1","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#installation","content":"Installation"},"852":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-2","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#examples","content":"Examples"},"853":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-3","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#default","content":"Default"},"854":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-4","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading",